 Are you someone who enjoys detailed problem-solving, interrogating data, and rigorously assessing system performance? Do you get excited by technical challenges and collaborating on creative solutions with a digital mindset? If so, this could be the job for you.
 We are looking for a university student interested in a placement year in industry. You will design and conduct tests on fuel and landing gear avionics test benches and support our flight test analysis activities.
 Our Fuel Systems Test Analysis team is part of the transnational "Hydrogen Propulsion & Hydro-Mech Systems" Sub-Domain. We are all part of the Flight and Integration Test Centre, where we test the integration of the complete aircraft. This is reflected in our ways of working, allowing you to interact and build relationships with colleagues across Europe and across all aircraft systems.
 We are a product-focused community with a history of delivering innovation to our company. As a team, we conduct development testing of new aircraft systems through agile test methods, help to resolve in-service problems, and provide design feedback for future aircraft.
 What you will be doing: 
 As an intern with us, you will contribute to the delivery of Fuel Systems Test Team's mission:
 Support certification through integrated lab, rig and flight testing and analysis;
 Establish and improve the maturity of AC systems through the collaboration with other engineering teams;
 React to and help resolve in-service system issues;
 Aim for product safety beyond certification requirements;
 Implement synergies and alignment between rig and flight test.
 Every day will present a new challenge, you will test and improve your skills on a variety of activities including Lab Testing, Flight Test Analysis and Data Analytics.
 Lab Testing:
 Agreement on Lab Test Requirements, definition and validation of test benches;
 System level testing of landing gear functionality;
 In-service investigation by reproducing events on avionics benches;
 Preparing Lab Test Results Analysis.
 Flight Test Analysis:
 Agreement on Flight Test Requirements;
 Definition and validation of Flight Test Instrumentation;
 Support development and flight testing by following flights live through telemetry facilities;
 Preparing Flight Test Results Analysis and certification documentation.
 Data Analytics:
 Use of big data techniques to achieve cross-correlation between design, test rig and flight behaviour;
 Algorithm development using flight test data for monitoring, design feedback and support to in-service investigations, possibly in collaboration with other areas of engineering;
 Development of tools to support data analysis activities.
